{"hash":"a983e81af978e9a9","voice":"en-IN-NeerjaExpressiveNeural","rate":"+4%","dur":88.1,"said":"Feel the air change as the tunnel takes us underground. Down here, hear the oldest story of Mahakal, from the Shiva Purana. In an age long before kings wrote their names on stone, in the city then called Avanti, there lived a learned Brahmin named Vedapriya. He had four sons, and he raised them in the worship of Shiva. Every day the brothers shaped a linga out of earth and worshipped it with love. Far away, on the mountain Ratnamala, lived a demon named Dushana, made mighty by a boon from Brahma. He could not bear the Vedic worship, and he sent his daityas to stop it. Fear spread through the city, and his army closed in on the four brothers. They did not run. Calm and unafraid, they went on worshipping their little earthen linga. And then, beside that linga, the ground split open. Out of the earth rose Shiva, in a terrible form. ‘I am Mahakala,’ he declared, ‘risen up against the wicked.’ With a single sound, ‘Hum’, he burned Dushana to ash. The brothers begged him to stay and protect them for ever, and he stayed, as Mahakaleshwar. Walk on. Just ahead the tunnel opens, and you will see him.\n\nDid you know? The Shiva Purana says the holiness of Mahakal’s linga spreads for about three kilometres all around it.","segments":[{"key":"text","start":0,"end":1107},{"key":"didYouKnow","start":1123,"end":1226}],"words":[[0.098,0.361,0,4],[0.471,0.144,5,8],[0.627,0.228,9,12],[0.867,0.457,13,19],[1.336,0.156,20,22],[1.504,0.12,23,26],[1.637,0.349,27,33],[1.997,0.349,34,39],[2.358,0.168,40,42],[2.538,0.721,43,54],[4.147,0.349,56,60],[4.507,0.325,61,65],[5.084,0.276,67,71],[5.373,0.168,72,75],[5.553,0.433,76,82],[5.998,0.349,83,88],[6.358,0.168,89,91],[6.538,0.613,92,99],[7.392,0.24,101,105],[7.644,0.084,106,109],[7.74,0.325,110,115],[8.077,0.553,116,122],[9.531,0.12,124,126],[9.663,0.144,127,129],[9.82,0.3,130,133],[10.132,0.312,134,138],[10.457,0.325,139,145],[10.793,0.325,146,151